So we know it's there. Now how to access it. The admin profile panel is susceptible to SSTI (server side template injection), which we can check by seeing if it'll follow a math command rather than just plaintext.

Referencing https://medium.com/@bootstrapsecurity/server-side-template-injection-ssti-advanced-exploitation-techniques-2d8ccdf6270f for SSTI injection types, we just need to decipher how to extract the contents of the flag folder. After searching around a bit, I found that you can utilize the passthru command to search the databases (even hidden/forbidden) for possible files. By inputting the command {{ ['find -type f -name "*.txt" 2>/dev/null','']| sort('passthru')|join }}, we can search for any text files on the server and return them as our new username. And with the newfound file address, we can pull the document directly off the site without having to access the files folder directly, giving us our final flag.

